hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20938","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban informed us from Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab from his father that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about fasting, so he said: Fast one day of every month. He asked him for more, so he said: By my father and mother, I find myself strong, so increase me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I find myself strong, I find myself strong, so he would not increase him. He asked him for more, so he said: Fast two days of every month. He said: By my father, you and my mother, O Messenger of Allah, I find myself strong. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I find myself strong, I find myself strong, so he would not increase him. When he pressed him upon it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fast three days of every month."
"20939","Affan narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab say: My father asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about fasting, so he said: Fast one day of every month. He said: O Messenger of Allah, by my father and mother, increase me. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says: Increase me, increase me. Fast two days of every month. He said: O Messenger of Allah, by my father and mother, increase me, for I find myself strong. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says: I find myself strong, I find myself strong, I find myself strong. He said: So he held back, meaning he refrained, until I thought he would not increase me. He said: Then he said: Fast three days of every month."
"20940","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us from Humayd, meaning Ibn Hilal, who said: A man from al-Tufawah whose road was upon us came to the tribe and narrated to them, he said: I came to Madinah with a caravan of ours, we sold our goods, then I said: I will go to this man and bring to those after me news of him. He said: I reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was showing me a house. He said: A woman was in it, she went out in an expedition of the Muslims and left twelve goats of hers and her spindle she wove with. He said: She missed a goat of her sheep and her spindle, so she said: O Lord, You have guaranteed whoever goes out in Your path that You preserve for him, and I have missed a goat of my sheep and my spindle, and I adjure You for my goat and my spindle. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began mentioning the severity of her supplication to her Lord, blessed and exalted. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In the morning her goat and its like, and her spindle and its like. And those, go to her and ask her if you wish. He said: I said: Rather I believe you."
